cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ampliscan in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ampliscan: an anchor-based amplicon demultiplexer with a desktop GUI for barcode-tagged sequencing reads"
abstract: >-
  ampliscan is a lightweight Python package that demultiplexes amplicon
  sequencing reads by inner, anchor-flanked barcodes carried on custom PCR
  primers. It locates a user-defined pair of constant anchor sequences, reads
  the variable barcode adjacent to each, and assigns every read (or read pair)
  to the corresponding sample bin, matching the anchor and barcode together as
  a single octanucleotide unit. The same engine is exposed through a scriptable
  command-line interface and a zero-dependency desktop GUI.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-23"
license: MIT
